/*****************************************************************************
    jitJE -- `if` WITH NO ELSE ARM. The shape no rung had.

    J2 covers if/else. NOTHING covered a bare `if cond; body;`, and that gap hid
    a dominance violation for as long as the emitter has existed: jitIfElse moves
    the insert point into elseBB while gJitResult still holds THE THEN ARM'S
    value, so with no else to overwrite it the commit landed a then-block value
    inside the else block --
        else:  store i32 %sub, ptr %result      ; %sub is defined in `then`
    llvm::verifyFunction refused the function outright, so this was never a wrong
    ANSWER; it was a REFUSAL TO RUN. Found 2026-08-01 while probing recursion.

    ⚠ THE INJECTIVITY HERE IS ABOUT THE BRANCH, not just the value. Fire 1 takes
    the then arm, fire 2 must NOT -- and the two answers must differ, or a
    constant would satisfy both. jeIn 5 -> then runs -> jeOut 50; jeIn 0 -> then
    skipped -> jeOut keeps the value the statement BEFORE the if put there (7),
    which is also the assertion that an absent else contributes NO value rather
    than a zero or a stale one.
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(JitLadder);
define
    jeIn;
    jeOut;
    jitJE code={ jeOut = 7; if jeIn > 1; jeOut = jeIn * 10; };
    ;

jeIn  = 5;
jeOut = 0;
print "JE fire 1 setup : jeIn =" jeIn:;
testing(jitJE);
print "JE fire 1 result: jeOut =" jeOut " (want 50 -- then arm taken)":;

/*  ⚠ NO RECOMPILE. The condition flips, so fire 2 proves the BRANCH is decided
    at run time and that the absent else leaves the slot alone.  */
jeIn  = 0;
jeOut = 0;
print "JE fire 2 setup : jeIn =" jeIn " (recompile: NONE)":;
jitRefire();
print "JE fire 2 result: jeOut =" jeOut " (want 7 -- then arm SKIPPED)":;

jeIn  = 5;
jeOut = 0;
jitJE();
print "JE interpreted  : jeOut =" jeOut " (the oracle -- want 50)":;
print "JE SENTINEL":;
stop();
